    "text": "Oklahoma City Comets edged 5-4 by Reno Aces; Jack Suwinski goes hitless\nBy\nS. I. ArceThe Oklahoma City Comets, with former Taft High School IL standout Jack Suwinski on the roster, suffered a 5-4 defeat against the Reno Aces in MiLB play on Tuesday, June 23, at 9:35 p.m.\nThe game was held at Greater Nevada Field, marking the seventh contest between the teams this season. The Comets now lead the season series 4-3 over the Aces.\nSuwinski recorded no hits in 4 at-bats, struck out twice, and stranded 4 runners on base.\nThe Comets are set to face the Aces again at Greater Nevada Field on Wednesday, June 24.\nJack Suwinski — Outfielder — 6â€²1â€³ — 217 — Hometown: Chicago",
